[patterns/application/micro-frontend/PTN-APP-MFE-009-shell-provided-props-pattern.md#technical-context]

### Technical Context

**Application Architecture:**
- Shell application: React 18+ with authentication integration
- Micro-frontends: 6-10 modules loaded dynamically via Module Federation
- Identity Provider: OAuth2/OIDC (Azure AD, AWS Cognito)
- Configuration Service: Backend API providing feature flags, environment config

**Current State:**
```typescript
// ❌ PROBLEM: Each module fetches independently

// claims-mfe/src/App.tsx
function ClaimsApp() {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);
  const [config, setConfig] = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    fetchUser().then(setUser);        // Redundant API call #1
    fetchConfig().then(setConfig);    // Redundant API call #2
  }, []);

  if (!user || !config) return <Loading />;
  return <ClaimsContent user={user} config={config} />;
}

// provider-mfe/src/App.tsx
function ProviderApp() {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);
  const [config, setConfig] = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    fetchUser().then(setUser);        // Redundant API call #3
    fetchConfig().then(setConfig);    // Redundant API call #4
  }, []);

  if (!user || !config) return <Loading />;
  return <ProviderContent user={user} config={config} />;
}

// Result: 4+ API calls for same data, inconsistent timing
```

