[patterns/application/micro-frontend/PTN-APP-MFE-009-shell-provided-props-pattern.md#variation-2-lazy-context-initialization]

#### Variation 2: Lazy Context Initialization

**Use Case**: Modules that don't need all context data immediately; fetch additional data lazily.

**Implementation:**

```typescript
// shell/src/bootstrap.tsx
export async function bootstrapApplication(): Promise<MfeContext> {
  // Fetch only critical data immediately
  const user = await authService.getCurrentUser();

  // Lazy-load feature flags and config
  const lazyConfig = {
    get config() {
      return configService.getAppConfig();  // Fetches on first access
    },
    get featureFlags() {
      return configService.getFeatureFlags();
    },
  };

  return {
    user,
    ...lazyConfig,
    theme: { mode: 'light', primaryColor: '#0066cc', fontFamily: 'Inter' },
  };
}
```

**Trade-offs:**
- ✅ Faster bootstrap time (fetch only critical data)
- ✅ Modules that don't need config don't pay the cost
- ❌ More complex implementation (lazy getters)
- ❌ Potential for race conditions if multiple modules access lazy props simultaneously

