[patterns/application/micro-frontend/PTN-APP-MFE-009-shell-provided-props-pattern.md#variation-3-multi-level-context-providers]

#### Variation 3: Multi-Level Context Providers

**Use Case**: Different module groups need different context subsets (e.g., admin modules need additional permissions).

**Implementation:**

```typescript
// shell/src/App.tsx
export function App() {
  const [baseContext, setBaseContext] = useState<MfeContext | null>(null);
  const [adminContext, setAdminContext] = useState<AdminContext | null>(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    // Fetch base context for all modules
    bootstrapApplication().then(setBaseContext);

    // Fetch admin-specific context if user has admin role
    if (user?.roles.includes('Admin')) {
      fetchAdminContext().then(setAdminContext);
    }
  }, []);

  return (
    <>
      {/* Standard modules receive baseContext */}
      <Route path="/claims/*" element={<MicroFrontend name="claims" context={baseContext} />} />

      {/* Admin modules receive extended context */}
      <Route path="/admin/*" element={<AdminMicroFrontend name="admin" context={{ ...baseContext, ...adminContext }} />} />
    </>
  );
}
```

**Trade-offs:**
- ✅ Separation of concerns (admin context separate from base context)
- ✅ Security (non-admin modules never see admin props)
- ❌ Increased complexity (multiple context types)
- ❌ Requires different mount function signatures for admin modules

